# AI Search Router — Project Rules (Concise)

## Purpose

Browser extension that routes searches to AI engines or traditional SERPs using fast, deterministic query classification (no ML/LLM).

**What it does**

- Classifies queries locally in <1ms
- Sends questions/complex queries → AI search
- Sends factual/navigation queries → traditional SERP
- Users pick providers or use custom URLs (`{query}` placeholder)

## Monorepo

```
/
├─ packages/
│  ├─ core/        # @ai-search-router/core (classifier + providers)
│  └─ extension/   # @ai-search-router/extension (shared WebExtension)
└─ platforms/
   ├─ chromium/    # Chrome/Edge/Brave build
   └─ safari/      # Xcode wrapper (future)
```

Managed with pnpm workspaces. Core is reused by extension; extension is reused by platforms.

## Core Library (`packages/core`)

- `classifyQuery(query: string): 'ai' | 'serp'`
- Provider presets and URL helpers

### Classification Rules (ANY → 'ai')

1. Contains W-words anywhere: `who`, `what`, `where`, `when`, `why`, `how`
2. Starts with: `is`, `if`, `can`, `could`, `should`, `would`, `will`, `do`, `does`, `did`
3. Contains `?`
4. Contains `,` or `;` (multi-part/complex)
5. Has "but/and + question word" pattern (e.g., "but are", "and can")
6. Word count ≥ 10
   Otherwise → `'serp'`

### Providers

AI:

- Google AI Mode: `https://www.google.com/search?udm=50&q={query}`
- Perplexity: `https://www.perplexity.ai/search?q={query}`
- ChatGPT: `https://chat.openai.com/?q={query}`

SERP:

- Google: `https://www.google.com/search?q={query}`
- Kagi: `https://kagi.com/search?q={query}`
- Qwant: `https://www.qwant.com/?q={query}`
- DuckDuckGo: `https://duckduckgo.com/?q={query}`

Defaults: AI = Google AI Mode, SERP = Google
Custom URLs supported (uses `{query}` substitution with URL-encoding).

## Extension (`packages/extension`)

- MV3 service worker intercepts searches
- Loads preferences from storage
- Calls `@ai-search-router/core` for classification
- Redirects to the selected provider URL

Permissions: `storage`, `tabs`, `webNavigation` or `declarativeNetRequest`

## Dev Workflow

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm -r build     # build all
pnpm -r dev       # watch mode
pnpm -r test      # tests
```

Chromium build:

```bash
cd platforms/chromium
pnpm build  # outputs to platforms/chromium/dist/
```

Load unpacked at `chrome://extensions` → Developer mode → Load unpacked → `platforms/chromium/dist/`

## Testing

- Core unit tests: `packages/core/src/*.test.ts`
- Verify: common patterns, edge cases, URL formatting, perf (<1ms)
- Manual extension checks: toggle works, provider persistence, custom URL usage, classification preview, redirection across entry points

## Conventions

- TypeScript strict; no `any`
- `kebab-case` files, `PascalCase` types, `camelCase` vars
- Absolute imports within packages; import core as `@ai-search-router/core`

## Notes

- Do not auto-start dev servers; check first
- All logic is client-side; no backend
- Preferences stored locally (not synced by default)
